  "body": "### Description\r\n\r\nReloading synapse config doesn't seem to reload the ratelimit config\r\n\r\n### Steps to reproduce\r\n\r\n- update `rc_message` config in homeserver.yaml\r\n- `kill -HUP $synapse_pid`\r\n- send messages and still run into the same ratelimiting\r\n\r\nThe following was printed in synapse log which indicates that the config was indeed reloaded\r\n```\r\nJul 06 20:57:34 bubu systemd[1]: Reloading Synapse Matrix homeserver.\r\nJul 06 20:57:34 bubu systemd[1]: Reloaded Synapse Matrix homeserver.\r\n```\r\nAfter actually restarting synapse afterwards the new ratelimits did apply\r\n\r\n### Version information\r\n\r\n- **Homeserver**: matrix.bubu1.eu\r\n\r\n<!--\r\n What version of Synapse is running?\r\n\r\nYou can find the Synapse version with this command:\r\n\r\n$ curl http://localhost:8008/_synapse/admin/v1/server_version\r\n\r\n(You may need to replace `localhost:8008` if Synapse is not configured to\r\nlisten on that port.)\r\n-->\r\n- **Version**: 1.16.0rc2\r\n\r\n- **Install method**:archlinux package built for latest rc\r\n\r\n<!-- examples: package manager/git clone/pip  -->\r\n\r\n- **Platform**: Archlinux",
